module std.witness_purpose

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }
import std.content_hash { ContentHash }
import std.measure { Millisecond, ByteSize }

type WitnessResourceBound
  = EvalWallTimeBound { bound: Millisecond }
  | EvalThreadCpuBound { bound: Millisecond }
  | PeakMemoryBound { bound: ByteSize }

// ResourceContract bound is axis-typed: wall/cpu limits are Millisecond; peak memory is ByteSize
// (std.measure). A single Millisecond field on all axes was state-space conflation — PeakMemory
// with a millisecond bound was writable. Aligns with discrete_cost derivation section 10 bound:
// Measure; full Measure coproduct lands when the cost consumer derives bounds.

// DECLARED witness purpose taxonomy (operator ruling 2026-08-04; DESIGN
// witness-cost-derives-from-purpose; discrete-cost-derivation section 10). What semantic fact the
// witness exists to prove — authored, not inferred from implementation. Cost and placement are
// DERIVED consequences on ScheduledWitnessEnvelope (std.realization_schedule SpanEnrolled), not
// here. Slice C-a lands only this stable vocabulary; placement and envelope derivation are separate
// slices.

// TerminatingOneShot is NOT a writable WitnessPurpose arm in slice C-a. It demands a pinned
// subject, a mechanically checkable dissolution trigger, AND a typed deadline after which an
// undissolved survey REFUSES — without the deadline substrate every permanent witness can claim to
// be a one-shot. A NonEmptyStr deadline field that always routes to OneShotUnavailable is rung
// inflation: a named future capability wearing the clothes of a finished arm.
// TerminatingOneShotFrontier records honest unavailability until std.measure lands typed
// instant/deadline and completion-receipt carriers; then TerminatingOneShot joins WitnessPurpose
// and this frontier type deletes.

// WHAT A BEHAVIORAL DISCRIMINATOR REQUIRES OF THE DECISION IT WATCHES, and the reason this is a
// REFINEMENT of BehavioralDiscriminator rather than a sixth peer arm (operator ruling, 2026-09-02).
// The bare arm said only "this witness discriminates behaviour", which is true of a discriminating
// RED and of an accepted positive control equally -- so it could not order a population by which
// rows carry a wall. DESIGN 4b(1) already names these as the two halves of executed evidence: a
// discriminating RED refused on the real acceptance path, PLUS an accepted positive control. This
// type is that pair, authored.
//
// WHY THE DISTINCTION IS A SAFETY FACT AND NOT A LABEL. A row requiring a refusal is GREEN in the
// ordinary case, so when it does not execute -- preempted, skipped, undecided -- the wall it
// carries is switched off with nothing red anywhere, and a later green over that absence is a
// green over a refusal that did not run. A row requiring an acceptance, not executing, leaves a
// question open and removes no wall. Same terminal state, different consequence, and until this
// payload existed nothing in the tree could tell them apart. The class is
// `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `non_execution_undifferentiated_by_what_it_silenced`.
//
// THE SUBJECT IS THE DECISION, NEVER THE WITNESS. Both arms name the decision the row watches --
// the function or declaration that must refuse or must admit -- so the fact is joinable against
// that decision rather than being an adjective on the test. A payload naming the test itself would
// restate the identity the row already has and could not be checked against anything.
//
// AUTHORED, NOT INFERRED, which the module header already requires of purpose and which binds here
// specifically: a lens could observe that a test body matches a refusal-shaped variant, and that
// observation is NOT this fact. It would make the compiler's own reading of the body the authority
// on what the body is for, so a body that stopped requiring the refusal would silently restate its
// own purpose instead of going red.
type DiscriminatedOutcome
  = RefusalRequired { refuser: DeclarationRef }
  | AcceptanceRequired { acceptor: DeclarationRef }

type WitnessPurpose
  = BehavioralDiscriminator { discriminates: DiscriminatedOutcome }
  | BoundaryCrossing { modeled_boundary: DeclarationRef, chosen_input: ContentHash }
  | PopulationTotality { population: DeclarationRef }
  | ExternalFidelity { effect: DeclarationRef }
  | ResourceContract { bound: WitnessResourceBound }

type TerminatingOneShotFrontier
  = TerminatingOneShotUnavailableDeadlineSubstrateAbsent
  | TerminatingOneShotUnavailableCompletionSubstrateAbsent
